<p class="hint tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>How depreciation is estimated</h2>
<p>The calculator uses straight-line depreciation, age divided by expected life, capped at the maximum you choose. Real estimates may use condition adjustments, different life tables or non-depreciable items, so treat the result as a planning figure.</p>
<h2>Common life expectancies in estimates</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Common range</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>3-tab asphalt shingles</th><td>20–25 years</td></tr><tr><th>Laminated shingles</th><td>25–30 years</td></tr><tr><th>Steel siding</th><td>40–50 years</td></tr><tr><th>Vinyl siding</th><td>30–40 years</td></tr><tr><th>Seamless gutters</th><td>20–30 years</td></tr><tr><th>Interior paint</th><td>8–12 years</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2>Getting holdback released</h2>
<p>Most policies release recoverable depreciation after repairs are complete within a time limit. Send invoices and photos of finished work, and set a reminder with the <a href="/claim-calculators-kansas/claim-timeline-builder/">claim timeline builder</a>.</p>

<h2>Questions about this calculator</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary><span>Should labor be depreciated?</span><svg class="pl" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Practices vary by policy and jurisdiction. Ask your insurer to explain its approach in writing and check how your estimate treats labor.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>What if I don’t repair?</span><svg class="pl" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Under most replacement cost policies you keep the ACV payment but may not recover the held-back depreciation.</p></div></details></div>
